llvm-3.7.1 forward port: the compiler-made init and destroy functions get a definition's attributes

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for every function clang makes through
CodeGenModule::CreateGlobalInitOrDestructFunction (`__cxx_global_array_dtor`,
`__cxx_global_var_init`, `_GLOBAL__sub_I_<file>`, `__dtor_<var>`,
`__tls_init`): 3.7.1 gives them the attributes of a declaration
(SetLLVMFunctionAttributes), so under -fstack-protector-strong and with
unwind tables they have neither `sspstrong` nor `uwtable`; upstream gives
them a definition's (SetInternalFunctionAttributes). The base's array-destroy
helpers are a definition's code (68 rows of the game module: `push rbp;
mov rbp, rsp` first, as in a function with unwind tables, where 3.7.1's
object has the body's first load between the two).

Three upstream commits, each whole (tests left out), all first released in
3.8.0, applied with offsets only (fuzz 1 on two CGBlocks.cpp hunks):
  r249722 (200500d6d3bf, 2015-10-08) "[CodeGen] Check if the Decl pointer
    passed is null, and if so, return early": the prerequisite:
    SetLLVMFunctionAttributesForDefinition takes a null declaration (the
    stack protector attributes move above the early return);
  r249735 (aec6b2c20e48, 2015-10-08) "[CodeGen] Attach function attributes
    to functions created in CGBlocks.cpp": the prerequisite's other half:
    SetCommonAttributes, setNonAliasAttributes and every target's
    setTargetAttributes take a null declaration (without it r251734
    dereferences one: round 270B's crash); its four block-helper call sites
    come with it and no C++ unit reaches them;
  r251734 (7791f1a4a952, 2015-10-31) "[CodeGen] Call
    SetInternalFunctionAttributes to attach function attributes to internal
    functions": the change itself, with the CGFunctionInfo passed in by each
    of the eleven callers.

Swept alone over the game module built by the installed 3.7.1 (round 273B,
5,496 rows, 6,656 functions): 75 functions change; 68 rows become equal
(5,297 to 5,365), the 68 array-destroy helper rows, and none is lost.

